<.shell title="Navigation" current={:navigation}>
  <h1>Navigation</h1>
  <p class="lead">How people move between and within pages.</p>

  <h2>Top bar</h2>
  <p>
    Navy, with the amber rule and logo. It holds the main sections and the account menu. The
    current section is underlined in amber.
  </p>
  <div class="demo bar-demo" style="padding: 0">
    <Web.Layouts.main_nav_bar
      current_user={sample_user()}
      current_team={sample_team()}
      current_path="/teams/squamish/activities"
    />
  </div>
  <p class="spec">
    In the app: the layout's <code>main_nav_bar</code>, built from <code>&lt;.site_bar&gt;</code>, with the account menu open here.
  </p>

  <h3>On a phone</h3>
  <p>
    Below 1024px the sections, Admin, and the account menu move behind a Menu button. The
    panel opens under the amber rule, the width of the screen, with the current section
    marked in amber. Going to another page closes it.
  </p>
  <div class="demo phone-width phone-bar-demo" style="padding: 0">
    <Web.Layouts.main_nav_bar
      current_user={sample_user()}
      current_team={sample_team()}
      current_path="/teams/squamish/activities"
    />
  </div>
  <script>
    // Open the menus, so the examples show them.
    document.querySelectorAll(".bar-demo .site-bar-menu, .phone-bar-demo .site-bar-phone")
      .forEach(function (menu) { menu.open = true; });
  </script>

  <h2>Menu</h2>
  <p>A short list under a button, such as the account menu above.</p>
  <p class="spec">
    Keep menus for a few links that do not fit in the bar. Actions on a page are buttons.
  </p>

  <h2>Breadcrumbs</h2>
  <div class="demo">
    <.breadcrumbs team={sample_team()}>
      <:item label="Members" path="#" />
      <:item label="Avery Chen" />
    </.breadcrumbs>
  </div>
  <p class="spec">
    On every page below a section's list. The last item is the current page and is not a link. In the app:
    <code>&lt;.breadcrumbs team=&#123;@current_team&#125;&gt;</code>
    with an <code>&lt;:item label="…" path=&#123;…&#125; /&gt;</code>
    for each level.
  </p>

  <h2>Back link</h2>
  <div class="demo">
    <p>
      <.a href="#">← Squamish SAR</.a>
    </p>
  </div>
  <p class="spec">
    For pages outside the main tree, like settings, instead of breadcrumbs. In the app: an
    <code>&lt;.a&gt;</code>
    whose text starts with ←, as on the team settings page.
  </p>

  <h2>Tabs</h2>
  <div class="demo">
    <.tabs label="Member">
      <:tab navigate="#" current>Attendance</:tab>
      <:tab navigate="#">Qualifications</:tab>
      <:tab navigate="#">Groups</:tab>
      <:tab navigate="#">ID card</:tab>
      <:tab navigate="#">History</:tab>
    </.tabs>
    <p>Each tab is its own page with its own URL, so links and the back button work.</p>
  </div>
  <p class="spec">
    In the app: <code>&lt;.tabs label="Member"&gt;</code>
    with a <code>&lt;:tab navigate=&#123;…&#125; current&gt;</code>
    for each page. <code>current</code>
    marks the page you are on.
  </p>

  <h2>Pagination</h2>
  <div class="demo">
    <div class="table-summary">
      <span class="table-summary-count">1,912 activities</span>
    </div>
    <.pagination paginated={sample_page()} path_fn={fn _ -> "#" end} />
  </div>
  <p class="spec">
    Under long tables, and only when there is more than 1 page. In the app: <code>&lt;.pagination paginated=&#123;@paginated&#125; path_fn=&#123;@path_fn&#125; /&gt;</code>, with the
    <code>App.Page</code>
    from <code>Repo.paginate/2</code>. Prefer filters that shrink the list over paging through it.
  </p>
</.shell>
